  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "All new external finishes in respect of all the works hereby approved (and any other incidental works to be carried out in this connection) shall match the existing building in respect of materials used, detailed execution and finished appearance, unless otherwise stated on the drawings hereby approved.REASON: To ensure that the external appearance of the building is satisfactory and does not detract from the character and visual amenity of the area.",
    "The lower ground floor and upper ground floor rear extensions hereby approved at Nos. 32 and 34 Castlewood Road shall be constructed as one building operation and neither extension shall be occupied until the other nears practical completion.&nbsp;REASON: To safeguard the amenity of the neighbouring residents.",
    "Prior to occupation of the development hereby approved, a minimum of two bee nesting bricks and two Swift nesting bricks and/or boxes shall be provided. The Swift nesting bricks and/or boxed should be placed at least 5m above the ground with a 5m unobstructed flight path, both below and in front of the swift brick. The Swift bricks and/or boxes should not be placed immediately above doors or windows. The bee and Swift bricks/boxes shall be retained thereafter in perpetuity.REASON: To support bird populations, including swifts, in Hackney and preserve endangered urban biodiversity, by providing nesting opportunities, in accordance with Hackney’s Local Plan LP33 policy LP47 which states that all development schemes involving buildings with an eaves height or roof commencement height of 5 metres and above are required to provide nesting boxes for swifts, sparrows, starlings, as appropriate.",
    "&lt;p&gt;The 1.1m high balustrading as shown on drawings&amp;nbsp;PR - P002 Rev B &amp;amp;&amp;nbsp;PR - P007 Rev B hereby approved shall be installed prior to the first use of the terrace and retained in perpetuity.&amp;nbsp;REASON: To safeguard the privacy and residential amenity of the occupiers of neighbouring properties.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The roof of the extension (other than designated amenity spaces) hereby approved shall not be used as a terrace, balcony or similar amenity area.\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\nREASON: In the interests of neighbours amenity\r\n&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
